          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.286,
            0.12,
            0.884,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "same one roti, each child gets a smaller share. So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " roti is more than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\textstyle { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } } \\; r o t i ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 12 > 14"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.199,
            0.72,
            0.225
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.1 Fractional Units and Equal Shares"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.242,
            0.66,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Beni: Which fraction is greater — "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 9 } ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.268,
            0.884,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Arvin: 9 is bigger than 5. So I would guess that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 9 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is greater than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 5 } . \\mathrm { A m }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " I right?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.314,
            0.884,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Beni: No! That is a common mistake. Think of these fractions as shares."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.356,
            0.884,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Arvin: If one roti is shared among 5 children, each one gets a share of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " roti. If one roti is shared among 9 children, each one gets a share of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{9}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " roti?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.424,
            0.821,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Beni: Exactly! Now think again - which share is higher?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.448,
            0.837,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Arvin: If I share with more people, I will get less. So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\textstyle { \\frac { 1 } { 9 } } < { \\frac { 1 } { 5 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.472,
            0.406,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Beni: You got it!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.388,
            0.511,
            0.649,
            0.543
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{Oh,~s0~\\frac{1}{100}~is~bigger~than~\\frac{1}{200}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.558,
            0.884,
            0.601
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When one unit is divided into several equal parts, each part is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "fractional unit",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". These are all fractional units:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.609,
            0.561,
            0.64
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{5}, \\frac{1}{6}, \\ldots, \\frac{1}{10}, \\ldots, \\frac{1}{50}, \\ldots, \\frac{1}{100}, \\text { etc. }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.649,
            0.83,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We also sometimes refer to fractional units as ‘"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "unit fractions",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.682,
            0.353,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.712,
            0.524,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fill in the blanks with fractions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.735,
            0.883,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Three guavas together weigh 1 kg. If they are roughly of the same size, each guava will roughly weigh ____ kg."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.782,
            0.809,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. A wholesale merchant packed 1 kg of rice in four packets of equal weight. The weight of each packet is ___ kg."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.825,
            0.809,
            0.888
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Four friends ordered 3 glasses of sugarcane juice and shared it equally among themselves. Each one drank glass of sugarcane juice."
            }
          ]
        },
